\begin{remark}[Mode-wise picture; origin modes in the risk
analysis]\label{rem:modewise}
Lemma~\ref{lem:origin} records the strongest smoothing at the origin
(gain $\asymp\delta_\lambda^{2}$ radially, and $\gtrsim\delta_\lambda^{2}$
for origin-near modes by \eqref{eq:origingain}) while the annulus bulk of
Lemma~\ref{lem:scale2} has gain $\asymp\delta_\lambda$. In §(C) only the
\emph{lower} bound of \eqref{eq:infsup} is inverted, and only on the
annulus bulk (gain $\asymp\delta$); origin-near modes have a comparable
or larger gain and are never inverted, so no two-sided estimate for them
is needed. Hence the risk analysis uses the annulus two-sided estimate
together with \eqref{eq:origingain}, valid for all $\alpha>1$, $d\ge2$
\end{remark}
